00:47:22,105 --> 00:47:28,105
Kutu Ma Kutu, also known as Kutu Ma Kutu Supari Dana (Nepali:कुटुमा कुटु or कुटुमा कुटु
सुपारी दाना) is a Nepalese song from the 2017 Nepalese film Dui Rupaiya.

11
00:52:06,315 --> 00:52:12,315
The song is sung by Rajan Raj Shiwakoti, Melina Rai and Rajan Ishan, with
lyrics and music by Prashidhika Tiwari, directed by Asim Shah.

12
00:56:50,526 --> 00:56:56,526
The music video of the track features actors Asif Shah,
Nischal Basnet, Swastima Khadka and Buddhi Tamang.

13
01:01:34,736 --> 01:01:40,736
On 22 December 2017 Kutu Ma Kutu became the first Nepalese YouTube video to reach 100 million views and it is the most viewed Nepalese video on YouTube currently
viewing over 200 million times, also it was the fastest song to gain 20 million views and in 49 days the song managed to gain 10 Million views.

14
01:06:18,947 --> 01:06:24,947
The name "Kutu Ma Kutu" is a Neologism that refers as the word kutu kutu mean something
that is hard when chewing it and the word supari dana means Areca nut.

15
01:11:03,157 --> 01:11:09,157
The word is usually used to invite someone to a function than
you chew the nut to accept the invitation.

